{
  "verso": "1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "DAG Notebook",
    "defaultKernel": "csharp",
    "activeLayout": {
      "extensionId": "com.verso.showcase.dag-notebook",
      "layoutId": "dag-notebook"
    },
    "extensions": {
      "required": [
        "Verso.Showcase.DagNotebook"
      ]
    }
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "da600000-0001-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "# DAG Notebook\n\nThis notebook uses the **DAG Notebook** layout (`Verso.Showcase.DagNotebook`, installed automatically the first time you open it). It looks and works like the regular notebook, with one addition: cells that share variables are linked.\n\n- A chip like `↑ 2 unitPrice` means this cell reads `unitPrice` from cell 2; `↓ 4 revenue` means cell 4 reads `revenue` from this one. Click a chip to jump to the linked cell.\n- When a cell finishes running, the cells downstream of it re-run automatically, in dependency order.\n- A cell whose inputs ran more recently than it did shows a dashed border until it catches up.\n\nRun everything once with **Run DAG** in the header, then try the experiment further down."
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0002-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "// The base inputs. Everything below derives from these two values.\nvar unitPrice = 24.99;\nvar unitsSold = 1200;\nConsole.WriteLine($\"{unitsSold} units at {unitPrice:C}\");"
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0003-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "var revenue = unitPrice * unitsSold;\nConsole.WriteLine($\"Revenue: {revenue:C}\");"
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0004-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "var costRatio = 0.62;\nvar profit = revenue * (1 - costRatio);\nConsole.WriteLine($\"Profit: {profit:C}\");"
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0005-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "var summary = $\"Sold {unitsSold} units for {revenue:C}, keeping {profit:C} in profit.\";\nConsole.WriteLine(summary);"
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0006-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Try it\n\nChange `unitPrice` in cell 2 to `29.99` and run just that cell. Revenue, profit, and the summary re-run on their own, in order. Then toggle **Auto-run dependents: Off** in the header and repeat: this time the downstream cells only mark themselves stale (dashed border) and wait for you.\n\n## When the layout refuses to guess\n\nThe two cells below both assign `counter`, so there is no single producer to link. Each gets a warning chip instead of an edge, and `counter` never participates in auto-run."
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0007-4000-8000-000000000007",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "var counter = 0;"
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0008-4000-8000-000000000008",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "counter = counter + 1;\nConsole.WriteLine($\"counter is now {counter}\");"
    }
  ]
}
